  "ticker_map_notes": {
   "2026-08-13": "Added SMCI / PLTR / CORZ, all verified via yfinance symbol search (NMS common stock; for Core Scientific this means CORZ, deliberately NOT the CORZW warrants or CORZR/CORZZ variants). These are EXITED historical positions -- the ticker_map had been seeded from CURRENT holdings, so any name the user once held and fully sold was absent. That is why the 2025-2026 backfill agents had to quarantine 12 confirmations they had extracted perfectly: they were correctly refusing to infer a ticker from email subject text (TICKER INTEGRITY), and the map simply had no entry. Seeding the map from current holdings alone is the underlying defect; a historical pull will keep hitting it for every exited name. EXTENDED: window 1 (2025-04-30..07-31) quarantined 21 more rows across Apple -> AAPL and Penguin Solutions -> PENG (both NMS, verified via symbol search) on top of SMCI/PLTR/CORZ. Five exited names, 33 correctly-extracted confirmations held back solely for a missing map entry. This is now a measured systemic cost of seeding ticker_map from current holdings, not an anecdote. FURTHER EXTENDED by window 4 (2026-02..04), which quarantined 24 more rows across 8 names. Six now verified and added: WDC, RMBS, FLNG (NYQ), FCG (PCX ETF), LLY (NYQ), FSLR. Palantir was already added. 'Pure Storage, Inc.' (5 rows) is DELIBERATELY LEFT UNRESOLVED -- see known_gaps G67. RESOLVED BY THE USER: 'Pure Storage, Inc.' -> P (NYSE) and 'SpaceX' -> SPCX (NASDAQ). Both verified after the fact: P's profile states outright that the company 'was formerly known as Pure Storage, Inc. and changed its name to Everpure, Inc. in February 2026' (same Santa Clara address, same Purity/FlashArray/FlashBlade lines), which is precisely why PSTG returns 'Quote not found' and why INDmoney kept emailing the old display name through the Feb-Apr 2026 trades. SPCX resolves to Space Exploration Technologies Corp. Both display-name variants mapped for each, old and new."
  },
