 "changes": [
  {
   "date": "2026-07-22",
   "summary": "NOW fully exited; BABA new position (5sh, 1.42% wt, ticker freshly resolved); AMAT cut to dust (2.009->0.0092sh); QCOM increased 6->14sh; GLW trimmed 19->10sh; CIEN trimmed 3.39->1.39sh; GEV rebuilt from dust to 1sh. Value $40,834.49 (+5.03% vs 07-20), new peak, drawdown 0%. Cash breach severe (1.11% vs [3,15]%), AI-capex breach 98.58% vs 90% cap, both structural (not market-driven). smith-rebound failed twice (stalled), degraded gap. Strategist proposed SNDK trim (~$1,500) + ORCL full exit (~$530) to address both breaches; held IREN/GEV adds despite bullish theses given the cash/capex constraint."
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-07-23",
   "summary": "Only real flow: GEV bought up further (1.0008->1.3950sh, +$394, wallet-funded), same day thesis downgraded strengthening->watch on Q2 EPS miss (revenue beat, guidance raised). Wallet nearly exhausted ($457.77->$36.14). Total book $41,923.47 (+2.67% vs 07-22). NEW G3-variant incident: INDmoney price feed fabricated +10-20% gains on ~10 names, discarded, yfinance used instead (G22). smith-rebound succeeded this run (G21 resolved) -- 5 macro-driven stage-in candidates (GEV/VRT/LITE/COHR/META), but cash math only funds one (VRT) after restating SNDK trim + ORCL exit as prerequisites."
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-07-24",
   "summary": "MAJOR FLOW EVENT: LITE, META, GOOG, BABA, STM fully exited; AMD trimmed 2->1sh; QCOM trimmed 14.0008->6.0008sh. Confirmed real via wallet-cash reconciliation ($36.14->$5,656.86). STM crashed -18.67% intraday (presumed earnings, unconfirmed). GOOG -6.89% (unexplained). Book now 24 positions, equity value $35,655.38 (-14.6% vs 07-23), total book incl. wallet roughly flat (-1.1%). AI-capex concentration hit 100.0% (worst ever) as BABA's exit removed the last non-AI-capex sleeve. SNDK breaches 12% single-position cap (13.271%). AI Memory/Storage cluster breaches over-band (31.502%); Networking/Optics, Power/Cooling/DC Infra, and Compute/Hyperscaler clusters all breach UNDER-band for the first time (fewer names spreading the same bands thinner). Drawdown -14.878%, 0.12pt from the 15% warn threshold -- closest this book has come to risk-off. Cash $5,656.86 (13.693%) sits inside policy band for the first time in weeks. Strategist proposed: trim SNDK ~$1,000, deploy GEV ~$900, deploy COHR ~$700, hold remaining ~$5,057 cash given 4 earnings prints next week (GLW/TER 07-28, QCOM/LRCX 07-29) and drawdown proximity to warn threshold. No genuine AI-capex diversifier found in watchlist output (BABA/SNPS both AI-adjacent, IBM flagged value-trap). ORCL: fresh oversold-bounce (real $7B DoD contract) vs standing breakdown/debt flags -- strategist verdict hold, no action, though two PRIOR open proposals (07-22, 07-23) had recommended exiting ORCL entirely -- unresolved inconsistency, flagged."
  },
